Q: Wordpress Multisite www non-www Page Redirect Failure A: <p>Try adding the following to your <code>wp-config.php</code>:</p>
<pre class="lang-php prettyprint-override"><code>define( 'NOBLOGREDIRECT', 'http://example.com' );
</code></pre>

Q: How can I fix a dropdown menu that is misaligned and overlapping in Elementor ElementsKit? A: <p>The problem you are experiencing is the result of applying <strong>position: absolute;</strong> to <strong>menu-header-menu</strong>. You can fix it by deleting that line or replacing <strong>absolute</strong> with <strong>flex</strong>.
<div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false" data-babel-preset-react="false" data-babel-preset-ts="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-css lang-css prettyprint-override"><code>.navbar {
    position: fixed;
    top: 0;
    width: 100%;
}

ul#menu-header-menu {
    position: flex;
    z-index: 9999;
    top: auto;
}</code></pre>
